1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,093
Forty tests.

2
00:00:01,093 --> 00:00:02,769
One hundred percent coverage.

3
00:00:02,769 --> 00:00:08,199
I flipped one character in the payment logic, greater-than to greater-than-or-equal, and every

4
00:00:08,199 --> 00:00:10,048
single one of them still passed.

5
00:00:10,848 --> 00:00:11,482
I'm Hajin.

6
00:00:11,482 --> 00:00:13,954
The world doesn't need another AI demo.

7
00:00:13,954 --> 00:00:19,849
In 2026 about a quarter of merged commits carry AI traces, coding agents write the tests too,

8
00:00:19,849 --> 00:00:24,984
and the one number we use to gate releases doesn't move when the tests get worse.

9
00:00:26,384 --> 00:00:29,622
This is live at killscore dot hajin dot xyz right now.

10
00:00:29,622 --> 00:00:31,362
Nothing here is pre-rendered.

11
00:00:31,362 --> 00:00:36,519
KillScore takes the pull request diff, finds only the functions it touched, and plants

12
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:37,958
deliberate bugs in them.

13
00:00:37,958 --> 00:00:42,756
Then it runs your own test suite against every mutant in an isolated subprocess.

14
00:00:42,756 --> 00:00:44,015
Twenty-seven mutants.

15
00:00:44,015 --> 00:00:45,814
Coverage stays at one hundred.

16
00:00:45,814 --> 00:00:47,973
Mutation score lands at sixty-three.

17
00:00:47,973 --> 00:00:50,792
Ten bugs your tests would let straight through.

18
00:00:51,892 --> 00:00:53,643
Here's the one that matters.

19
00:00:53,643 --> 00:00:56,331
This is a boundary check in the tier logic.

20
00:00:56,331 --> 00:00:59,082
We changed it, and forty tests still passed.

21
00:00:59,082 --> 00:01:00,458
No model decided that.

22
00:01:00,458 --> 00:01:03,646
A subprocess ran your suite and read the exit code.

23
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:05,647
Now Claude writes a test for it.

24
00:01:05,647 --> 00:01:11,337
And before you ever see that test, our runner proves two things: it passes on the original,

25
00:01:11,337 --> 00:01:13,025
and it fails on the mutant.

26
00:01:13,025 --> 00:01:13,900
Verified kill.

27
00:01:19,852 --> 00:01:21,487
Let me show you it failing.

28
00:01:21,487 --> 00:01:24,454
Here the model's test fails on the original code.

29
00:01:24,454 --> 00:01:29,418
It encoded a wrong expectation, which is exactly the failure we're gating against.

30
00:01:29,418 --> 00:01:31,417
Rejected, and queued for a human.

31
00:01:31,417 --> 00:01:32,809
And this one timed out.

32
00:01:32,809 --> 00:01:34,262
A timeout is not a kill.

33
00:01:34,262 --> 00:01:37,108
Counting it as one would inflate our own score.

34
00:01:38,792 --> 00:01:39,730
Six components.

35
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:43,981
Exactly one is a model call, and its output never touches the score.

36
00:01:43,981 --> 00:01:48,607
The model never marks a mutant killed and never edits the code under test.

37
00:01:48,607 --> 00:01:49,857
Seven seconds a run.

38
00:01:49,857 --> 00:01:54,608
Zero dollars for the score, about a cent and a half when you ask for a test.

39
00:01:55,408 --> 00:02:01,121
Twenty copies of a billing module, each with one planted bug and an AI-written suite at one

40
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,690
hundred percent coverage.

41
00:02:02,690 --> 00:02:04,386
The suite alone caught six.

42
00:02:04,386 --> 00:02:06,834
A model reading the code caught twelve.

43
00:02:06,834 --> 00:02:08,592
KillScore surfaced nineteen.

44
00:02:08,592 --> 00:02:14,493
And after adding only the tests our runner verified, the mutation score went from seventy-five

45
00:02:14,493 --> 00:02:15,498
to ninety-seven.

46
00:02:15,498 --> 00:02:16,816
Coverage never moved.

47
00:02:17,916 --> 00:02:20,246
The gate turns that into a merge check.

48
00:02:20,246 --> 00:02:25,744
Set a threshold, name the paths where no survivor is acceptable, and the pull request gets a

49
00:02:25,744 --> 00:02:29,568
GitHub check and an evidence PDF with a hash over every verdict.

50
00:02:29,568 --> 00:02:30,823
Free on public repos.

51
00:02:30,823 --> 00:02:35,364
Ninety-nine dollars a month for the release engineer who has to press merge.

52
00:02:36,164 --> 00:02:36,918
KillScore.

53
00:02:36,918 --> 00:02:39,932
Live now at killscore dot hajin dot xyz.

